<title>USA: Mich. $383 mln agency notes repriced, yld 3.80 pct.</title>
<headline>Mich. $383 mln agency notes repriced, yld 3.80 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc. said Tuesday it repriced Michigan Municipal Bond Authority's $383 million revenue note deal. The one-year notes due July 2, 1998, yielded 3.80 percent at the repricing.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>MICHIGAN MUNICIPAL BOND AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $382,505,000*</p>
<p>REVENUE NOTES</p>
<p>SERIES 1997B</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: NAF		 S&amp;P: SP-1+</p>
<p>    DATED: 07/02/1997	  FIRST COUPON:</p>
<p>DUE: 07/02</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>07/02/1998	    382,505M    4.50  %	  3.80</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 100.674)</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected</p>
<p>Delivery is firm for July 2, 1997.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry.  DTC is pending.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>Comerica Securities - Detroit</p>
<p>First Chicago Capital Markets, Inc.</p>
<p>M.R. Beal &amp; Company</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley Dean Witter</p>
<p>PaineWebber Incorporated</p>
<p>Prudential Securities Incorporated</p>
<p>Smith Barney Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
